{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-021-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"20Dt³","working":"Velocity is the first derivative of position: v(t)=x'(t)=5Dt⁴−E. Acceleration is the derivative of velocity: a(t)=v'(t)=20Dt³. The constant −E has derivative zero, so it does not appear in the acceleration.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":433,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":49,"cacheReadTokens":384},"outputTokens":381,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":90,"reasoningTokens":291},"totalTokens":814,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":433,"completion_tokens":381,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":384,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":49,"total_tokens":814,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":384},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":291}},"reasoningTokens":291,"cachedInputTokens":384},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3958,"keyed_label":"A"}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-018-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"D","final_answer":"2F₀L/3","working":"The work done by a variable force along the x-axis is W = ∫ F(x) dx from x=0 to x=L. Substitute F(x)=F₀(1 − x²/L²): W = F₀ ∫₀ᴸ (1 − x²/L²) dx = F₀ [x − x³/(3L²)] from 0 to L = F₀ (L − L³/(3L²)) = F₀(L − L/3) = 2F₀L/3.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":458,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":74,"cacheReadTokens":384},"outputTokens":282,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":151,"reasoningTokens":131},"totalTokens":740,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":458,"completion_tokens":282,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":384,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":74,"total_tokens":740,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":384},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":131}},"reasoningTokens":131,"cachedInputTokens":384},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":2879,"keyed_label":"D"}
{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-018-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"D","final_answer":"2F₀L/3","working":"The work done by a one-dimensional force F(x) moving an object from x = 0 to x = L is given by the integral W = ∫₀ᴸ F(x) dx. Substituting F(x) = F₀(1 - x²/L²): W = ∫₀ᴸ F₀(1 - x²/L²) dx = F₀ [x - x³/(3L²)]₀ᴸ = F₀(L - L³/ (3L²)) = F₀(L - L/3) = 2F₀L/3.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":397,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":397,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":416,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":160,"reasoningTokens":256},"totalTokens":813,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":256,"promptTokenCount":397,"candidatesTokenCount":160,"totalTokenCount":813,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":397}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":160}]},"reasoningTokens":256,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3831,"keyed_label":"D"}
