{"key":"u13-apphycm-mcq-027-v1","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"26 J","working":"Work done by a one-dimensional variable force F(x) moving an object from x_1 to x_2 is given by W = \\int_{x_1}^{x_2} F(x) dx. Here, F(x) = 3.0x^2, x_1 = 1.0 m, and x_2 = 3.0 m. Evaluating the integral: W = \\int_{1.0}^{3.0} 3.0x^2 dx = [x^3]_{1.0}^{3.0} = (3.0)^3 - (1.0)^3 = 27 - 1 = 26 J.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":398,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":398,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":438,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":186,"reasoningTokens":252},"totalTokens":836,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":252,"promptTokenCount":398,"candidatesTokenCount":186,"totalTokenCount":836,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":398}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":186}]},"reasoningTokens":252,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3651,"keyed_label":"B"}
